    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I'm looking for some help with my Monstera deliciosa. It's been sitting in my living room for a year and doing great, but lately, the lower leaves are starting to turn a pale yellow color. The soil feels kind of damp even when I think I've watered it, but I don't see any obvious pests. Any idea what might be going on?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The yellowing lower leaves, combined with damp soil, strongly suggests overwatering is the issue. Too much moisture deprives the roots of oxygen, leading to root rot which causes leaf discoloration. Try allowing the top several inches of soil to dry out completely between waterings to encourage better drainage.",
