    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for the tip about the bark and perlite. i'll grab some this weekend. one more thing though... i've noticed these weird little dark spots on the stems too, almost like they're being nibbled on? it's super weird because i haven't seen any bugs flying around. it almost feels like something is happening in the soil that i just can't see. is there anything else i should be looking for to make sure it's not something more serious?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Those dark spots could be signs of fungal issues or even some soil-dwelling pests like fungus gnats or mealybugs that are hard to spot. Carefully inspect the base of the stem where it meets the soil, looking for tiny insects or fine webbing. If you suspect pests, employing sticky traps or treating the soil surface with beneficial nematodes can help manage what's unseen underground.",
      "source": "target",
